<title>USA: St Joseph hogs up $2.00 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs up $2.00 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Compared to Tuesday, barrows and gilts $2.00 higher. CME delivery and packers putting out sharply higher bids and hoping that with a break in the weather hogs will start moving. Top 54.00. - USDA</p>
<p>US 1-3	230-270 lbs    53.50-54.00</p>
<p>Sows:  Scarce.</p>
<p>Pkg US 2-3	570 lbs    52.00</p>
<p>Boars:  Scarce.</p>
<p>Barrows and Gilts</p>
<p>SC    US 1-2    230-250 lbs    54.00-only</p>
<p>SG    US 1-3    230-250 lbs    53.50-54.00</p>
<p>SH    US 1-3    250-270 lbs    53.50-54.00</p>
<p>SL    US 2-3    250-270 lbs    53.50-54.00</p>
<p>SM    US 2-3    270-300 lbs    -----------</p>
<p>Sows</p>
<p>SW    US 1-2    300-400 lbs    ----------</p>
<p>SX    US 1-2    400-500 lbs    ----------</p>
<p>SY    US 1-3    500-600 lbs    ----------</p>
<p>SZ    US 1-3    600-700 lbs    ----------</p>
<p>Boars</p>
<p>TA		  300-700 lbs    ----------</p>
<p>Estimated Slaughter Hog Receipts:  200.</p>
